# 11. Quarter 1 Growth Check Design

The growth check is the Week 9 cumulative assessment. It should be treated with the same instructional framing as the Week 2 baseline: informative, not punitive.

## Purpose

- measure retention and transfer across all six Quarter 1 skills;
- provide a direct point of comparison to the Week 2 baseline;
- surface which skills need continued attention heading into Quarter 2.

## Recommended Length

**28–32 questions**

## Target Completion Time

**45–55 minutes**

This is intentionally longer than a single-week check, since it spans the entire quarter.

---

# 12. Growth Check Content Coverage

| Domain | Approx. Questions |
|---|---:|
| Numbers & operations | 4 |
| Fractions & decimals | 4 |
| Percent | 4 |
| Ratios, rates & proportions | 5 |
| Variables & expressions | 5 |
| Equations | 5 |
| Mixed / unlabeled application | 3–5 |

**Total:** 30–32 questions

