# 30. Day 4 — Quarter 1 Growth Check

## Before the Assessment

Remind students:

- this measures growth across the whole quarter, not just this week;
- some questions will not announce which skill they require;
- attempting unfamiliar-looking questions still provides useful information;
- they should use the Week 2 problem-solving routine (STOP → FIND → CONNECT → TRY → CHECK) throughout.

## Student Task

Complete the 28–32 question Quarter 1 Growth Check.

## After the Assessment

If time remains, students complete an initial reaction:

- Which questions felt most familiar?
- Which questions felt hardest to identify, not just hardest to solve?

