# 31. Day 5 — Analyze Results and Set a Quarter 2 Goal

## Mini-Lesson

Revisit the five error categories and the Strength / Developing / Priority language from Week 2.

## Student Task

Students review their Growth Check results and complete the Week 9 Quarter 1 Reflection (Section 34), including:

- their strongest skill, with evidence;
- a developing skill, with evidence;
- a priority skill, with evidence;
- their most frequent error type across the quarter, with evidence;
- one specific, actionable goal for Quarter 2.

## Teacher Role

Circulate and help students connect specific missed questions to specific error types, rather than defaulting every miss to "I'm bad at math."

## Study Hall / Catch-Up

Remaining time can be used for:

- incomplete work;
- academic organization;
- current coursework;
- teacher conferences on Growth Check results.

