# 35. Differentiation — Students Requiring Support

Provide:

- the Quarter 1 Skill Map as a constant visual reference during retrieval days;
- worked examples alongside each retrieval block;
- smaller, more frequent retrieval sets rather than one large mixed set;
- sentence starters for the Quarter 1 Reflection;
- one-on-one review of Growth Check results before the student completes the reflection independently.

Support should help students access the same reflective process rather than simplifying it away.

---

# 36. Differentiation — Students Ready for Extension

Provide:

- additional unlabeled mixed-skill problems requiring recognition across two or more domains at once;
- a request to write their own mixed-skill word problem combining two Quarter 1 units;
- deeper error-pattern analysis across all four weekly checks (Weeks 3, 5, 7, 8) rather than a single tally;
- a written explanation of how one Quarter 1 skill will be used again in Quarter 2's Inequalities & Constraints unit.

Extension should emphasize synthesis across the quarter rather than simply more questions.

