# 37. Data to Collect

By the end of Week 9, collect:

- Growth Check accuracy, overall and by domain;
- Growth Check accuracy by question level (Recognize/Execute/Apply/Reason);
- direct comparison to Week 2 baseline results where parallel questions exist;
- self-identified strongest skill, developing skill, and priority skill;
- self-identified most frequent error type, and whether it matches teacher-observed patterns from Weeks 3–8;
- Quarter 2 goal statements.

This data set should directly inform Quarter 2 pacing and any small-group review before Week 10 begins.

