# 41. Transition to Week 10

Quarter 1 built the arithmetic and algebraic foundation: number sense, fractions, decimals, percent, ratios, rates, expressions, and equations.

Quarter 2, **Mathematical Reasoning** (October 26 – January 22), extends this foundation into new territory, beginning with:

# Week 10: Inequalities & Constraints

Students will work with:

- inequality symbols (`<`, `>`, `≤`, `≥`);
- translating verbal constraints into inequalities;
- solving simple inequalities;
- graphing solution sets;
- interpreting inequalities in context.

Solving an inequality uses the same inverse-operation logic as solving an equation, with one new rule: the direction of the inequality symbol reverses when both sides are multiplied or divided by a negative number. Week 10 should open by explicitly connecting this to Week 8's equation-solving process rather than presenting it as an unrelated new topic.

The academic cycle continues into Quarter 2 unchanged:

> **Learn → Practice → Check → Analyze → Retry → Apply**
